//! HUD / system-info scenes: coin pop-up, battery warning, error window.
//!
//! # What this module covers
//!
//! Three NW4R `lyt` scenes of `New SUPER MARIO BROS. Wii` that report system
//! state to the player. They were promoted from the staging lane
//! `src/subsystems/r80014_80040.rs` (entry range `0x80014000..0x80040000` of
//! `sys/main.dol`); the 20 rows of that lane live here, plus the nine wave-7
//! point-get/battery/error helpers, the fifteen wave-12 counter, error-flow and
//! nunchuk-warning helpers, the nine wave-19 battery/error/nunchuk bodies, the
//! seven wave-21 state-table/nunchuk bodies, the seven wave-26 nunchuk
//! release/animation-start bodies, the twenty-three wave-32
//! `dWarningOther`/`dWarningYoKo` state-table, constructor, layout and
//! teardown bodies, the twenty-six wave-90 four-player slot and teardown
//! bodies, the thirty wave-96 wipe-transition bodies, the twenty-six wave-101
//! panel-update, wipe-gate and record-accessor bodies, the six wave-107
//! wipe-follow, sprite-record and `daikonbou` model bodies, and the one
//! wave-113 course-select guide state-table initialiser.
//!
//! | Cluster | Original entries | Content |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `pointGet` coin pop-up | `0x80014F10..0x800151D0` | [`fn_80014f10`], [`fn_80014ff0`], [`fn_80015160`], [`fn_800151d0`] |
//! | `batteryInfo` low-battery warning | `0x80015D60..0x80016870` | [`fn_80015d60`], [`fn_80015e80`], [`fn_80015ec0`], [`fn_80015f90`], [`fn_80016020`], [`fn_80016210`], [`fn_800162c0`], [`fn_800163f0`], [`fn_800166b0`], [`fn_800167b0`], [`fn_800167f0`], [`fn_80016870`] |
//! | `errorInfo` error/notification window | `0x80016F70..0x800175C0` | [`fn_80016f70`], [`fn_800171f0`], [`fn_80017340`], [`fn_800175c0`] |
//!
//! Each scene is a C++-shaped object: constructor, `dWarning*_c`-style state
//! machine, deleting destructor, and (for the two warnings) a small group of
//! window open/close helpers. The class names `dWarningBattery_c` and
//! `dWarningErrorInfo_c` are inferred from the RTTI strings used by the
//! neighbouring state-table builders at `0x80016A80` and `0x80018330`, which
//! are **not** translated in this pass.
//!
//! # Start here
//!
//! [`fn_80016020`] is the clearest entry point: it loads
//! `batteryInfo/batteryInfo.arc`, loads `batteryInfo_10.brlyt`, binds four
//! `.brlan` animations, eleven battery-bar panes, nine node panes, twenty
//! battery pieces and eight text panes, then initialises the four position
//! records. [`fn_800171f0`] is the same shape for the error window, and
//! [`fn_80014ff0`] for the small `pointGet` counter.
//!
//! # Dependencies
//!
//! - [`crate::platform`] for byte-wide target memory access and indirect calls.
//! - [`crate::ui::lyt`] for the NW4R layout primitives: the small-data anchors,
//!   the `lyt` callee table (`0x800C8xxx`/`0x800C9xxx`), [`vtable_method`],
//!   [`copy_vec3`] and the wide-call helpers. The full object model and the
//!   derivation of `r13`/`r2` are documented there and are not repeated here.
//!
//! `no_std`; no allocation in the reconstruction. Every "allocation" below is
//! an original callee that builds panes or animation objects in game memory.
//!
//! # Scene state at a glance (observed)
//!
//! | Scene | Layout | Built flag | Per-frame state |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | `pointGet` | `+0x04` | `+0x21D` | `+0x1F8` (`4` = ready) |
//! | `batteryInfo` | `+0x08` | `+0x284` | `+0x285` started, `+0x286..+0x289` per-player enabled, `+0x28A` window open |
//! | `errorInfo` | `+0x08` | `+0x22C` | `+0x22D`/`+0x22E` open/advance, `+0x220` selected button |
//!
//! Rendered objects are panes resolved from name tables; their visibility is
//! bit 0 of `pane + 0xBB` (`| 1` shows, `& 0xFE` hides), and the layout's
//! animations are addressed by index after binding.
//!
//! # What is still staged
//!
//! The lane's remaining work is **not** code in this module: the state-table
//! builders (`0x80016A80`, `0x80018330`), the coin motion update
//! (`0x80015C10`), the battery per-frame body (`0x80016430`) and the error
//! state-machine body (`0x80017630`) have no translation yet. They stay
//! listed as next targets in `docs/COVERAGE_r80014_80040.md`. The error open
//! animation (`0x800174C0`) was translated in wave 7.
//!
//! # Wave 3: battery and controller widgets (`0x80176410..0x801788C0`)
//!
//! The second pass added the battery/controller cluster that the home-button
//! overlay owns:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x80176410` | [`fn_80176410`] | map the controller battery level to the ten-segment gauge |
//! | `0x80176610` | [`fn_80176610`] | initialise the controller-info frame (audio/GX-independent state) |
//! | `0x80176740` | [`fn_80176740`] | show `N_Trans` + battery panes for connected players |
//! | `0x801786B0` | [`fn_801786b0`] | show the four battery-power panes of one player |
//! | `0x801788C0` | [`fn_801788c0`] | draw the battery gauge quad with the computed alpha |
//!
//! These bodies all operate on the home-button menu object (the same
//! `+0x238` layout owner, `+0x2AC` four player widgets and `+0x2F0` pane array
//! used by `crate::ui::menu`), not on a `batteryInfo` scene. The battery
//! *warning window* lives above in this file; this cluster is the battery
//! *indicator* inside the menu.
//!
//! # Wave 7: counter colours, battery open, error open/close
//!
//! The third pass adds the remaining small bodies around the two warning
//! scenes and the coin counter:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x80014F80` | [`fn_80014f80`] | release a `pointGet` scene |
//! | `0x80015210` | [`fn_80015210`] | write the counter colour pair through virtual slot `+0x28` |
//! | `0x800153B0` | [`fn_800153b0`] | write one digit colour into its record |
//! | `0x800154E0` | [`fn_800154e0`] | advance the counter tick and select the next digit slot |
//! | `0x80015580` | [`fn_80015580`] | flash the counter colour pair |
//! | `0x80015CE0` | [`fn_80015ce0`] | open the battery warning at a position and mode |
//! | `0x80016E80` | [`fn_80016e80`] | release an `errorInfo` record |
//! | `0x80017440` | [`fn_80017440`] | close the error window when it is open |
//! | `0x800174C0` | [`fn_800174c0`] | play the error open animation for the selected button |
//!
//! The colour tables live at fixed data addresses (`0x80351EA8`,
//! `0x80351EBC`, `0x80351ED0`) or in the SDA (`r13 - 0x5A70`); each is
//! initialised lazily behind a one-byte guard, exactly as in the original.
//!
//! # Wave 12: counter motion, error flow and nunchuk warning
//!
//! The fifth pass adds the remaining per-frame counter movement, the four
//! error-window state transitions, and the `extensionControllerNunchuk`
//! warning scene:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x800151F0` | [`fn_800151f0`] | destroy the `pointGet` layout at `+4` |
//! | `0x80015200` | [`fn_80015200`] | refresh one counter digit colour |
//! | `0x80015780` | [`fn_80015780`] | move and flash the coin-pop-up pane |
//! | `0x80015F20` | [`fn_80015f20`] | release one battery record |
//! | `0x800162E0` | [`fn_800162e0`] | destroy the `batteryInfo` layout at `+8` |
//! | `0x80016300` | [`fn_80016300`] | refresh the four per-player battery slots |
//! | `0x80017910` | [`fn_80017910`] | choose the next error-window animation |
//! | `0x80017A10` | [`fn_80017a10`] | start the error button/player animations |
//! | `0x80017A90` | [`fn_80017a90`] | notify when the button animation ends |
//! | `0x80017B20` | [`fn_80017b20`] | show the selected answer button |
//! | `0x80017D60` | [`fn_80017d60`] | start the confirm animation and timer |
//! | `0x80017DE0` | [`fn_80017de0`] | advance the error window after animation |
//! | `0x80018060` | [`fn_80018060`] | close the error window |
//! | `0x80018CA0` | [`fn_80018ca0`] | construct the nunchuk warning scene |
//! | `0x80018F20` | [`fn_80018f20`] | build the nunchuk warning layout |
//!
//! The two counter thunks (`0x800151F0`, `0x800162E0`) call the same NW4R
//! layout teardown, while `0x80015200` and `0x80015780` complete the digit and
//! position path started by [`fn_800154e0`]. The error bodies connect the
//! existing open/advance/close functions to the button panes `+0x204/+0x208`
//! and the timer `+0x21C`. The nunchuk scene is a third warning class shaped
//! like `errorInfo` but with its layout at `+4` and build flag at `+0x1E4`.
//!
