//! | `0x8001F6C0` | [`fn_8001f6c0`] | insert a value into the twelve-slot table |
//! | `0x8001F740` | [`fn_8001f740`] | remove a value from the twelve-slot table |
//! | `0x8001F800` | [`fn_8001f800`] | probe every slot and publish the manager word |
//!
//! All four scenes share one shape: a base object constructed through
//! `0x8016DC00` at `+0x00`, an NW4R layout at `+0x14`, the root pane at
//! `+0x1AC`, the pane resolution record at `+0x1B0`, a small state word at
//! `+0x1B4`/`+0x1BC`, the build flag at `+0x1B8`/`+0x1C0`, and the archive
//! plus `.brlyt` name at fixed data addresses. The four builders are the
//! callees that [`crate::engine::display`] reaches through its wipe gates, so
//! they are recorded here and the gate constants there stay one-way references.
//! The `wipeDokan` archive is the door transition (`dokan` = door).
//!
//! The four forwarding thunks repeat the `0x802DCBFC(b, b, a)` shape already
//! documented for `0x800182D0`; the twelve-slot table at `+0x0C..+0x38` holds
//! one entry per transition step and counts them at `+0x04`.
//!
//! # Wave 101: panel updates, wipe gates and record accessors
//!
//! The thirteenth pass clears the rest of this lane's `0x80010000` bucket: the
//! remaining four-player panel update bodies, the two wipe-scene gate bodies,
//! the last five `0x80377A04` accessors, the table-driven field copy at
//! `0x8001FF90`, two forwarding thunks and eight small record accessors.
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x800105B0` | [`fn_800105b0`] | read the SDA byte at `0x8042A24D` |
//! | `0x80010690` | [`fn_80010690`] | copy the widget translations into the four panes, reveal the last player |
//! | `0x80010800` | [`fn_80010800`] | restart the message animation of every changed channel |
//! | `0x80010950` | [`fn_80010950`] | close the four-player panel and reset its widgets |
//! | `0x80010B50` | [`fn_80010b50`] | select the message pane and animation for one message kind |
//! | `0x80010DD0` | [`fn_80010dd0`] | show or hide the three per-player message panes |
//! | `0x80012940`, `0x80012970` | [`fn_80012940`], [`fn_80012970`] | two `0x802DCBFC` forwarding thunks |
//! | `0x80014330`, `0x800148F0` | [`fn_80014330`], [`fn_800148f0`] | clear one word / three words of a record |
//! | `0x80014630`, `0x80014670`..`0x80014690`, `0x800146C0` | [`fn_80014630`], [`fn_80014670`], [`fn_80014680`], [`fn_80014690`], [`fn_800146c0`] | typed record field getters |
//! | `0x8001B580` | [`fn_8001b580`] | close a wipe scene |
//! | `0x8001B920` | [`fn_8001b920`] | advance the `wipeCircle` gate |
//! | `0x8001BA20` | [`fn_8001ba20`] | apply wipe mode `0`/`1` |
//! | `0x8001BF20` | [`fn_8001bf20`] | test the fade window against the frame delta |
//! | `0x8001CEE0` | [`fn_8001cee0`] | test a controller/warning pair |
//! | `0x8001DA80`..`0x8001DAC0` | [`fn_8001da80`], [`fn_8001da90`], [`fn_8001daa0`], [`fn_8001dab0`], [`fn_8001dac0`] | copies five to nine of the accessor |
//! | `0x8001FF90` | [`fn_8001ff90`] | copy the eight fields selected by `+0x5E4` |
//!
//! Two of these clusters overlap bands earlier passes assigned elsewhere:
//! `0x80010690..0x80010DD0` shares the cursor-panel fields (`+0x384..+0x3FC`,
//! `+0x408`, `+0x40C`, `+0x414`, `+0x44E`) with the `crate::game::path` bodies
//! and the widget fields (`+0x1A0`, `+0x218..+0x2CC`, `+0x434..+0x440`) with the
//! wave-90 bodies above, while `0x80014330..0x800148F0` are the record accessors
//! called from `crate::game::actor`. Both groups were still untranslated in
//! `ledger/functions.csv` when this pass ran and no other lane owns the bucket,
//! so they are recorded here and the other modules stay one-way references.
//!
//! # Wave 107: `wipeCircle` follow, HUD sprite records and `daikonbou`
//!
//! The fourteenth pass takes the six bodies wave 101 left as skips out of this
//! lane's `0x80010000` bucket:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x8001B620` | [`fn_8001b620`] | follow the current player with the `wipeCircle` pane |
//! | `0x8001E6F0` | [`fn_8001e6f0`] | position query, forwards a vector to slot `+0xC8` |
//! | `0x8001E790` | [`fn_8001e790`] | emit the nine-float record and trigger the hit effect |
//! | `0x8001F8A0` | [`fn_8001f8a0`] | release every populated slot of the twelve-slot table |
//! | `0x8001FA70` | [`fn_8001fa70`] | build the `daikonbou` model and its two animation records |
//! | `0x8001FD40` | [`fn_8001fd40`] | copy position and angles into the sprite record |
//!
//! Three of these close earlier clusters: [`fn_8001b620`] is the per-frame body
//! of the `wipeCircle` scene built by [`fn_8001b470`] and shares its
//! `+0x1AC`/`+0x1B4`/`+0x1C1` fields; [`fn_8001f8a0`] is the release pass over
//! the twelve-slot table of [`fn_8001f6c0`]/[`fn_8001f740`]; and
//! [`fn_8001e6f0`] reaches [`fn_8001e790`] through virtual slot `+0xC8` of the
//! `+0x60` vtable, which is why both signatures line up. That pass left
//! `0x800129A0` (6,204 bytes) untranslated, reading its 700 rendered lines as
//! opaque state data.
//!
//! # Wave 113: course-select guide state table (`0x800129A0`)
//!
//! The fifteenth pass translates the last entry of this lane's `0x80010000`
//! bucket, [`fn_800129a0`]. Ghidra prints it as 700 lines of `DAT_` stores, but
//! the body is 32 mechanically identical descriptor blocks and has been
//! reconstructed as the loop they encode:
//!
//! | address | Rust function | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x800129A0` | [`fn_800129a0`] | build the 32 `dCourseSelectGuide_c` state descriptors |
//!
//! The descriptors sit at `0x803516B8 + i*0x40`; their nine data words come
//! from `0x802FEB48 + i*0x24` in the fixed order `6,7,8,3,4,5,0,1,2`; the
//! shared vtable is `0x802FF63C` and the shared callback `0x80014240`. This is
//! the same descriptor protocol as the warning-scene table builders
//! [`fn_80016a80`]/[`fn_80018330`] above, with a different source layout and a
//! per-entry event word at `descriptor - 0x10`. A small preamble also fills
//! four `.data` words and the guide's guarded SDA pair; those roles are
//! unknown and stay labelled as such.
//!
//! # Glossary
//!
//! - **HUD** - heads-up display: the coin counter and the system warning
//!   windows drawn over gameplay.
//! - **NW4R / BRLYT / RLAN (BRAN)** - Nintendo Ware 4th generation layout
//!   system, its `.brlyt` layout files and `.brlan` animation files.
//! - **Pane** - a node of a layout tree; names use prefixes `T_` (text),
//!   `P_` (picture), `N_` (null/position), `A_`/`B_`/`C_` (window, button,
//!   player button).
//! - **vtable** - PowerPC function-pointer table; virtual calls here go through
//!   scene `+0x0C`/`+0x10` (layout) or `+0x1A0..+0x1AC` (member sub-objects).
//! - **SDA / `r13` / `r2`** - PowerPC small-data areas; see [`crate::ui::lyt`].
//! - **DOL** - the Wii executable container (`sys/main.dol`).

