///   `0x1F` sets `+0x680 = 2` unconditionally; afterwards the "held" branch
///   uses `0x1E` when `+0x68B == 1` and the child is not idle, and `0x1C`
///   otherwise, again setting `+0x680 = 2` on a hit.
