// ===========================================================================
// Wave 204, lane B: `0x80024F60..0x80026A90`
// ===========================================================================
//
// Module-doc addition for the merge pass (kept as `//` comments so that this
// file can be appended verbatim to `src/ui/hud.rs`):
//
// # Wave 204: pose refresh, arming state machine and object-release twins
//
// The seventeenth pass adds ten bodies of the `0x80024xxx..0x80026Axx` band:
// the pose-refresh body `0x80024F60`, the 508-byte arming state machine
// `0x80025800`, the vtable-assigning deleting destructor `0x80025F60`, three
// release/wrapper bodies that differ only in which destructor they run
// (`0x80026080`, `0x800260C0`, `0x80026850`), two literal accessors
// (`0x800268B0`, `0x800268C0`) and the animation-chain pair `0x800269B0` /
// `0x80026A90`.
//
// | address | Rust function | role |
// |---|---|---|
// | `0x80024F60` | [`fn_80024f60`] | refresh the pose flag, replay the walk animation, run two virtual slots |
// | `0x80025800` | [`fn_80025800`] | four-phase arming state machine over `+0x360` |
// | `0x80025F60` | [`fn_80025f60`] | install the `0x80329958` vtable, unlink, then optionally free |
// | `0x80026080` | [`fn_80026080`] | free-only release wrapper |
// | `0x800260C0` | [`fn_800260c0`] | `0x80168D80` release wrapper |
// | `0x80026850` | [`fn_80026850`] | `0x8015F800` release wrapper |
// | `0x800268B0`, `0x800268C0` | [`fn_800268b0`], [`fn_800268c0`] | literal `lis`/`addi`/`blr` accessors of `0x80357BF4` / `0x80357BB4` |
// | `0x800269B0` | [`fn_800269b0`] | walk up to five `+0x30` links, then recurse |
// | `0x80026A90` | [`fn_80026a90`] | compare the text after `':'` of two names |
//
// Three of the bodies are byte-identical to already translated ones and are
// documented as such rather than re-derived: `0x80026850` = `0x8001D710` =
// `0x8001F380`, `0x800269B0` = `0x8001D850` = `0x8001F4C0`, and `0x80026A90` =
// `0x8001D930`. `0x80025F60` is the twin of `0x80032A30`. Their repeated
// appearance is expected: the compiler emits one out-of-line copy per
// translation unit that only sees the class declaration.
//
// **Correction to the manifest.** `0x80025800` is listed as 16 bytes, but the
// entry is a full stack frame (`stwu r1,-0x20`, `stfd f31`, `psq_st f31`) that
// runs to the epilogue `bclr` at `0x800259F8`; the real extent is 508 bytes
// (`0x80025800..0x800259FC`). The disassembly, the Ghidra export and the
// `functions.tsv` prologue agree, so the body is translated in full.
//
// **Correction to the accessors.** The two 12-byte bodies in this lane are
// *not* the `0x80377A04` accessors of wave 203: raw words
// `3C608035 38637BF4 4E800020` and `3C608035 38637BB4 4E800020` are
// `lis r3,0x8035` / `addi r3,r3,0x7BF4|0x7BB4` / `blr`, i.e. `0x80357BF4` and
// `0x80357BB4`. The `0x80377A04` accessor of this band is `0x80026BB0`, which
// belongs to lane C.
//
// Addresses are `main.dol` runtime addresses.

