/// so the search depth is unbounded (a pure tail call that the compiler did
/// not convert to a `b`). The reconstruction keeps the unbounded walk as a
/// loop: same result, no host stack growth. Note that the non-zero arm returns
/// the *parent*, i.e. the check is made on the child but the parent is kept.
