// ===========================================================================
// Wave 205 (lane C): record accessors, child-chain search, name compare,
// two `0x802DCBFC` forwards and four `0x80377A04` accessors
// ===========================================================================
//
// The lane covers the ten bodies of the `0x8002C870..0x8002CBA0` run that
// closes the `0x8002A840..0x8002CBA0` helper family of `dScene`-shaped
// objects. Wave 204 lane F translated the head of that family
// (`0x8002A840..0x8002AC90`); this lane is the compiler-emitted second copy
// of the same shapes:
//
// | address | Rust function | role |
// |---|---|---|
// | `0x8002C870` | [`fn_8002c870`] | return `0x8035328C` (fourth record of the BSS table) |
// | `0x8002C880` | [`fn_8002c880`] | return `0x8035324C` (first record of the BSS table) |
// | `0x8002C970` | [`fn_8002c970`] | five-fold unrolled `+0x30` child-chain search, then recurse |
// | `0x8002CA50` | [`fn_8002ca50`] | compare the `':'` tails of two names |
// | `0x8002CB10` | [`fn_8002cb10`] | forward `(b, b, a)` with interface `a + 0x18` in `r12` |
// | `0x8002CB40` | [`fn_8002cb40`] | forward `(b, b, a)` with interface `a + 0x24` in `r12` |
// | `0x8002CB70` | [`fn_8002cb70`] | return `0x80377A04` |
// | `0x8002CB80` | [`fn_8002cb80`] | return `0x80377A04` |
// | `0x8002CB90` | [`fn_8002cb90`] | return `0x80377A04` |
// | `0x8002CBA0` | [`fn_8002cba0`] | return `0x80377A04` |
//
// Every body is byte-identical (modulo the `bl` displacement and, for the
// accessors, the immediate) to one already in `src/ui/hud.rs`, so the
// translations reuse the existing `DAT_*`, `FN_*` constants and helpers
// without redefining any of them:
//
