// Wave 205, lane D: the burst-actor teardown/probe band
// (`0x8002CBB0..0x8002DBD4`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// Ten bodies of the `Wm_en_burst_m` scene: two `0x80377A04` accessors, the
// `+0x524` buffer release, the `g3d/pakkun.brres` model builder that binds the
// `dokan_attack` clip, the two per-frame wrappers around `0x80095480`/
// `0x800954A0`, the sprite-transform writer (`0x8002D0C0`), the contact/damage
// body (`0x8002D480`), the four-slot "any live player" probe (`0x8002DAB0`) and
// the burst-death starter (`0x8002DB10`).
//
// Object map observed across the band (the same `+0x60` class vtable,
// `+0x394` layout-animation manager and `+0x544`/`+0x584` model records as the
// wave-204 door band that precedes it):
//
// | offset | type | role |
// |---|---:|---|
// | `+0x04` | `u32` | flags; bit 16 selects the `0x80097E50` sound arm |
// | `+0x60` | `u32` | class vtable (`+0x6C`/`+0x2D4` slots) |
// | `+0x7C` | record | sprite transform written by `0x8002D0C0` |
// | `+0xAC..+0xB4` | `f32 x3` | scene position |
// | `+0xD0`/`+0xD4` | `f32` | x/y contact offset triple |
// | `+0x100..+0x104` | `s16 x3` | sprite angle triple |
// | `+0x394` | manager | layout-animation manager (`+0x28`/`+0x14` slots) |
// | `+0x510` | `u32` | effect handle queried by `0x8009F6D0` |
// | `+0x524` | buffer | scratch transition buffer |
// | `+0x540` | `u32` | layout archive handle |
// | `+0x544` | `0x2C`-byte record | primary model record |
// | `+0x584` | `0x2C`-byte record | secondary animation record |
// | `+0x6AC` | `u32` | one-shot "died" latch |
// | `+0x6D4` | `s16` | second third-angle written by `0x8002D0C0` |
//
// `functions.tsv` reports
// `12/12/96/180/80/124/404/348/92/200` bytes; the prompt's `24` for
// `0x8002D0C0` disagrees with both the TSV row and the body: the prologue
// (`stwu r1,-0xB0`) and the `blr` at `0x8002D250` give a real extent of
// **404** bytes, which is exactly the TSV value, so `404` is used below. The
// two 12-byte accessors are the `lis`/`addi`/`blr` form, not prologue
// artefacts.
//
// `no_std`; every call is an original callee reached by address.

