///   extent is `0x30` (48 bytes) and matches `functions.tsv`. `r12` is computed
///   but never read by the callee, so the `+0x18` sub-object pointer is dead in
///   this build and is not reproduced.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `a`: object whose embedded descriptor supplies the `r12` interface.
/// - `b`: receiver forwarded in `r3` (the original `r5` copy is gone now).
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Whatever `0x802DCBFC` does; its jump table is not recovered.
///
/// # Safety
/// `a` must be a live object whose embedded descriptor is valid.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the operand permutation is literal, the callee is unresolved. The
/// body is byte-identical to [`fn_8001d9f0`], whose `r12` also carries `+0x18`.
pub unsafe fn fn_8003c990(a: u32, b: u32) {
    interface_call(a as usize, b, 0x18);
}

