// ===========================================================================
// Wave 208, lane C: the `togezo` step/init tail and the `0x8003Dxxx` helpers
// (`0x8003CCC0..0x8003DDF4`, ten bodies, 1,440 `functions.tsv` bytes /
// 1,596 verified)
// ===========================================================================
//
// The lane is the closing slice of the `togezo` (Spiny) scene whose release
// band, base destructor and model builder (`0x80037D20..0x800381B0`) were
// translated in wave 207 lane D, plus the small helper run that precedes it:
//
// | address | Rust function | role |
// |---|---|---|
// | `0x8003CCC0` | [`fn_8003ccc0`] | per-frame step: query, member teardown, `0x8003CF40`, `0x8003CE20`, dispatch |
// | `0x8003CE20` | [`fn_8003ce20`] | write the scene position/angle triple into the `+0x7C` sprite record |
// | `0x8003CF40` | [`fn_8003cf40`] | integrate one angle at `+0x102` from a rate and a per-frame count |
// | `0x8003D890` | [`fn_8003d890`] | release-and-free wrapper (twin of [`fn_80037d20`]) |
// | `0x8003D9D0` | [`fn_8003d9d0`] | walk up to five `+0x30` children through virtual slot `+0x0C`, then recurse |
// | `0x8003DAB0` | [`fn_8003dab0`] | compare the `':'`-tail of two names (twin of [`fn_8003c8d0`]) |
// | `0x8003DB70` | [`fn_8003db70`] | `0x802DCBFC` adjustor thunk, descriptor `a + 0x18` |
// | `0x8003DBA0` | [`fn_8003dba0`] | `0x802DCBFC` adjustor thunk, descriptor `a + 0x24` |
// | `0x8003DBD0` | [`fn_8003dbd0`] | build the `togezo` scene: `0x8003DCD0`, model builder, field block, slot `+0x300` |
// | `0x8003DCD0` | [`fn_8003dcd0`] | load `g3d/togezo.brres` + `g3d/paipo.brres` and bind four records |
//
// ## Sizes
//
// `functions.tsv` reports `120/236/16/92/224/136/48/48/228/292` bytes. Nine of
// the ten values are exact - each equals `entry .. blr + 4`, with no alignment
// padding in any row; `0x8003CF40` is a genuine prologue artefact in the
// `main` analysis (see its own doc block): `main-gb` records `172` for the same
// body and the closing `bclr` sits at `0x8003CFE8`, so the real extent is
// `0xAC` (172 bytes). Verified extents are therefore
// `0x78/0xEC/0xAC/0x5C/0xE0/0x88/0x30/0x30/0xE4/0x124`.
//
// ## Relation to bodies already in `src/ui/hud.rs`
//
// - `0x8003D890` is instruction-for-instruction the same release wrapper as
//   [`fn_80037d20`] and reuses `FN_8015F800`/`FN_802B9280`.
// - `0x8003D9D0` is the `bl 0x8003D9D0` target of the function at
//   `0x8003D8F0` (outside this lane), which contains the same five-level walk
//   unrolled; the shape is [`fn_8003c7f0`]'s.
// - `0x8003DAB0` is byte-identical to [`fn_8003c8d0`] and reuses
//   `FN_802E1C40`/`FN_802E1AB4`.
// - `0x8003DB70`/`0x8003DBA0` are two more copies of the `0x802DCBFC`
//   adjustor thunks [`fn_80037e40`]/[`fn_80037e70`] and reuse `FN_802DCBFC`.
// - `0x8003CE20` follows the same sprite-record sequence as [`fn_8001fd40`]
//   and reuses `FN_80064AF0`, `FN_801C0BD0`, the three angle setters,
//   `FN_8016A170`/`FN_8016A150`/`FN_8016A1A0` and `call_3f_1u`.
// - `0x8003DBD0` is the call site wave 207 lane D documented for
//   [`fn_800381b0`] (the `"togezo"`/`"g3d/togezo.brres"`/`"togezo_shell"`/
//   `0.0f` operands).
//
// Only three constants are new at module scope and all carry the `_C` suffix:
// `FN_8016A3A0_C`, the ten `togezo` string/table anchors and the six `f32`
// anchors of the `0x8042B6C0` pool.
//
// Addresses are `main.dol` runtime addresses; `r13` = `SDA_BASE` =
// `0x8042F680`, `r2` = `SDA2_BASE` = `0x80433080`.

