// ===========================================================================
// Wave 261, lane A (`_A261`): the first ten prologue-shaped targets of the
// `daEnTogezo_c` method table at `0x80306400`
// ===========================================================================
//
// The run at `0x80306400` is the largest uncovered function-pointer run in
// `0x80300000..0x80350000`: **193 consecutive words** of
// `0x80306400..0x80306703`, every one an in-image code pointer, every one
// **distinct** (no alias slots). It is bounded on both sides by a zero word
// (`0x803063FC`, `0x80306704`); the bytes immediately before it are the
// `togezo` resource strings (`"g3d/togezo.brres"` at `0x80306388`,
// `"togezo_shell"` at `0x8030639C`) and the bytes after it are the 12-byte
// `{ 0, -1, fn }` records (`0x8030670C`, ...).
//
// Shape evidence (`work/wave261/a/dump.mjs`, `extent.mjs`, `xref.mjs`,
// `xref_broad.mjs`):
//
// * **vtable, not a jump table.** A switch/jump table in this build contains
//   interior labels and repeated arms; here all 193 words are distinct
//   function *entry* points (36 of the 63 previously uncovered ones open with
//   `stwu r1,-N(r1)` + `mflr r0`, the rest with `blr` stubs, `b` thunks or
//   leaf-function heads), and slot 0 is [`fn_8003dbd0`], the `togezo` scene
//   builder. That is the layout of a class method table.
// * **No installation site in any shipped image.** No instruction in
//   `main.dol` builds `0x80306400..0x80306703` as a `lis`/`addi`/`ori`
//   immediate pair (even with a 200-instruction dataflow window), and no word
//   of `main.dol`, `d_basesNP`, `d_enemiesNP`, `d_en_bossNP` or `d_profileNP`
//   contains the table base as a raw pointer. The owning constructor therefore
//   installs it through a runtime-built descriptor, or the table is
//   shipped-but-dormant; the reference gap is recorded, not explained away.
// * 130 of the 193 slots were already covered (109 as untabled `fn_<address>`
//   bodies, 9 ledger `ui::hud` rows, 10 `game::stage`, 2 `game::player`).
//   The remaining 63 are the backlog; this lane translates the first ten in
//   slot order (`3, 6, 8, 9, 16, 22, 23, 27, 29, 33` -> 36 prologue-shaped
//   targets in total, as counted by `work/wave261/a/prologue.mjs`).
//
// The ten bodies are members of the shared `daEnNpBase_c`-style enemy actor
// documented above (`+0x60` class vtable, `+0x394` owner chain, `+0x348` side
// byte, `+0x7FC`/`+0x83C`/`0x878` sprite/animation nodes, `+0xAC..+0xB4`
// position, `+0xE8..+0xF0` motion triple, `+0x614..+0x63C` contact
// descriptor). `no_std`; every call is an original callee reached by address.
//
// ## Register findings worth keeping
//
// * `addi` immediates are signed: `0x80358004` is `lis 0x8036` +
//   `addi -0x7FFC`, and `0x802EE7D0` is `lis 0x802F` + `addi -0x1830`.
// * `0x80329958` in slot 16 is the 45-slot sub-object vtable already completed
//   in wave 260, confirming that the `+0x89C` member is that class.
// * The "boolean" normalization `neg/or/rlwinm` (and the `rlwinm rc` variant
//   used as a branch) reduces to `x != 0`; slot 27 applies it twice.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Callees and anchors introduced by this lane (suffixed `_A261`)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// `0x80065110(actor) -> u32`: the shared "contact mask fires" query.
const FN_80065110_A261: usize = 0x8006_5110;

/// `0x80065080(actor) -> u32`: the marker-sprite cull flag of
/// `crate::game::player`.
const FN_80065080_A261: usize = 0x8006_5080;

