/// vector `{table[side ^ 1] * 0.5, 2.0}` (table `0x8042C1B0`) and calls
/// `0x800A0EA0(this, object, vector, 0x80357BB4, 1)`; mode `3` calls
/// `0x800A1190(this, object, 1)`; any other mode does nothing.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: no export (untabled); Wave-226 corpus entry `0x80024340` (244 B).
/// - Evidence: `work/wave261/c/disasm.txt` slot 60; raw words `9421FFD0`,
///   `7C0802A6`, `90010034` at `0x80024340..0x80024348`.
/// - observed: `0x8002437C bl 0x80064A30`; `0x80024394 bl 0x800964A0`;
///   `0x800243AC bl 0x80095C20`; `0x800243D4 lfsx f1,r3,r0` against
///   `0x8042C1B0`; `0x800243E4 fmuls f0,f2,f1`; `0x800243FC bl 0x800A0EA0`;
///   `0x80024418 bl 0x800A1190`.
/// - observed: mode `1` uses index `side ^ 1` (`xori r0,r30,1`), unlike the
///   sibling [`fn_80024720`]/[`fn_800245a0`] which use `side` for the record
///   colour word.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: scene forwarded to every callee.
/// - `arg2`: opaque word forwarded as the predicate's and `0x80095C20`'s
///   second operand.
/// - `contact`: collision record; `+0x04` is the contact object.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing; the predicate result is only branched on.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One predicate call plus exactly one effect/reply call.
///
/// # Safety
/// `contact + 4` must hold a live object, and `0x8042C1B0`/`0x80357BB4` must
/// be readable.
///
