// ===========================================================================
// Wave 262, lane E (`_E262`): the first ten prologue-shaped bodies of the
// `0x80304E18` method array (`daEnKuriboBase_c` / `kuriboBig` scene)
// ===========================================================================
//
// The run `0x80304E18..0x803050FF` is a **186-slot method array**, the class
// vtable of the `kuriboBig` (Big Goomba) scene whose constructor and partial
// method set already live in this module (`fn_80033310`, `fn_800334f0`,
// `fn_80033650`, `fn_800337f0`, `fn_80033a30`, `fn_80033d40`, `fn_80034060`,
// `fn_80034140`, `fn_80034260`, `fn_800342f0`, `fn_80034380`, `fn_80034840`,
// `fn_80034a90`). The table address itself is `0x80304E10`: two zero header
// words (`0x80304E10`, `0x80304E14`) precede slot 0 at `0x80304E18`, and the
// word at `0x80305100` is the zero terminator of the run. The words after it
// (`0x288`, `0x60`, `0x284`, `0x60`, ...) are not code pointers.
//
// Shape evidence (`work/wave262/e_scan.mjs`, `e_table.mjs`, `e_shape.mjs`):
//
// * **186 consecutive slots, 186 distinct targets.** Every word points into
//   the executable image, every target is 16-byte aligned, and no two slots
//   are aliases, so this is a virtual-method array, not a state/jump table
//   (a jump table would contain interior labels and repeated arms).
// * Slots are **not** sorted by address: the targets span
//   `0x8001D1C0..0x801628B0` and mix inherited `dEn_c`/actor helpers with the
//   class's own `0x8003xxxx` bodies. Covered targets live in
//   `src/game/enemies.rs` (103), `src/game/stage.rs` (23),
//   `src/game/worldmap.rs` (7), `src/ui/hud.rs` (6) and
//   `src/game/player.rs` (4).
// * Census before this lane: **143 covered / 43 uncovered** distinct targets.
//   Of the 43, **24 open with a standard prologue** (`stwu r1,-N`, frames
//   `0x10`/`0x20`/`0x30`) and 19 do not: fifteen are one-word `blr` stubs
//   (`0x4E800020`) and four are leaf bodies (`0x80033440`, `0x80034D30`,
//   `0x800206D0`, `0x80034720`).
//
// This lane translates the first ten prologue-shaped targets in slot order
// (slots 0, 6, 9, 16, 21, 59, 61, 65, 68, 92):
//
// | slot | word | target | extent | role |
// |---:|---|---|---:|---|
// | 0 | `0x80304E18` | `0x80033230` | 208 B | scene init: model group, angle limit, state record |
// | 6 | `0x80304E30` | `0x80033450` | 104 B | owner tick + timed-burst query |
// | 9 | `0x80304E3C` | `0x800334C0` | 48 B | forward to the `+0x544` model's `+0x14` slot |
// | 16 | `0x80304E58` | `0x80034D40` | 200 B | deleting destructor |
// | 21 | `0x80304E6C` | `0x80034C70` | 52 B | transform refresh + bone rebind |
// | 59 | `0x80304F04` | `0x80033740` | 176 B | side/contact gate + state query |
// | 61 | `0x80304F0C` | `0x80033970` | 192 B | mode-2 collision dispatcher |
// | 65 | `0x80304F1C` | `0x80033DA0` | 232 B | contact reaction (mode 2 state) |
// | 68 | `0x80304F28` | `0x80033C50` | 240 B | contact reaction (mode 3 state) |
// | 92 | `0x80304F88` | `0x80034BC0` | 64 B | `"split"` clip bind + shared release tick |
//
// None has a `functions.tsv` row, a Ghidra export or a ledger row; every
// evidence line cites raw words in `work/dol/main.elf` (disassembly in
// `work/wave262/e_dis.txt`). Extents are measured to the terminating `blr`;
// each agrees with the `work/wave260/e_scan.txt` prologue census.
//
// Object map used below (same as the wave-206 lane D `kuriboBig` block):
// `+0x60` class vtable, `+0x120`/`+0x148`/`+0x518` init flags and model group,
// `+0x348` side byte, `+0x36D` ready byte, `+0x394` owner object, `+0x524`
// scratch buffer, `+0x540`/`+0x544`/`+0x584`/`+0x5C0` model and animation
