/// Gates on a signed travel distance, toggles the `+0x714` pose byte and
/// tail-dispatches virtual `+0x2D0`.
///
/// The `+0x348` target-pose byte selects which of the two travel constants is
/// added or subtracted from the `+0x708` base. The `+0xE8` signed coordinate
/// picks the sign: a non-negative value (or unordered, which the `cror`/`bc`
/// pair also sends down the negative arm) compares the `+0xAC` speed against
/// `base + offset`, a negative value against `base - offset`:
///
/// - target pose `0`, non-negative: `base + 0x6FC`, keep when `speed >=`;
/// - target pose `0`, negative: `base - 0x700`, keep when `speed <=`;
/// - target pose non-zero, non-negative: `base + 0x700`, keep when `speed >=`;
/// - target pose non-zero, negative: `base - 0x6FC`, keep when `speed <=`.
///
/// When the gate does **not** hold the body returns `0`. Otherwise `+0x714`
/// is XOR-ed with `1`, the new byte is stored, and slot `+0x2D0` runs with
/// `this`; its answer is returned.
