// ===========================================================================
// Wave 265, lane E (`_E265`): the first ten prologue-shaped bodies of the
// `0x80305F18` method array (`daEnShell_c`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// The run `0x80305F18..0x803061FB` is a **185-slot method array**, the class
// vtable of `daEnShell_c`. The table address is `0x80305F10`: two zero header
// words (`0x80305F10`, `0x80305F14`) precede slot 0 at `0x80305F18`, and the
// word at `0x803061FC` is the zero terminator of the run. The records that
// follow it (`0x288`/`0x60`, `0x284`/`0x60`, ...) are not code pointers.
//
// Shape evidence (`work/wave265/e_table.mjs`, `e_table.txt`):
//
// * **185 consecutive slots, 185 distinct text pointers.** No nulls, no
//   non-text words, no repeated targets, no interior labels of a tabulated
//   function; the targets span `0x8001D1B0..0x801628B0` and are not sorted,
//   so this is a virtual-method array, not a state/jump table.
// * Install site: there is no `lis`/`addi`/`stw` of `0x80305F10` in
//   `main.dol`. Four constructors in the `d_enemiesNP` REL materialise it
//   with `lis r4,0x8030` / `addi r4,r4,0x5F10` / `stw r4,0x60(r29)`:
//   REL virtual addresses `0x80A691C0`, `0x80A6A680`, `0x80B08760` and
//   `0x80B095E0` (`work/wave265/e_xref.txt`). The class word is therefore
//   installed at object `+0x60`; those constructors also initialise the
//   `+0x524` buffer and the `+0x544` sub-object. The table lives in the main
//   DOL data segment `0x802FE3A0..0x80351640`; no main-DOL relocation is
//   involved.
// * Class identity: the seven `daEnShell_c::StateID_*` descriptor strings sit
//   immediately before the header at `0x80305D83..0x80305E38`
//   (`Sleep`, `Carry`, `Slide`, `Wakeup`, `WakeupReverse`, `WakeupTurn`,
//   `DieFall`), between them and the header are `Wm_mr_kickhit`,
//   `g3d/daikonbou.brres`, `daikonbou`, `daikonbou_long` and
//   `Wm_ob_cmnspark`; `docs/UNTABLED_POINTER_TABLES.md` also names the table
//   as the `daEnShell_c` vtable.
// * Census at lane start: **146 covered / 39 uncovered** distinct targets
//   (`work/wave265/e_table.txt`). This is the correction to the wave-260
//   survey, which read 40 uncovered: waves 261-264 landed enough shared
//   `0x8003xxxx` base-class bodies to cover one more slot. The 12
//   prologue-shaped targets still match the survey exactly; the remaining 27
//   are 13 one-word `bl`/`blr` leaves and 14 non-prologue leaves. All 39
//   uncovered targets are in the `0x8003xxxx` band.
//
// This lane translates the first ten prologue-shaped targets in slot order:
//
// | slot | word | offset | target | extent | role |
// |---:|---|---:|---|---:|---|
// | 0 | `0x80305F18` | `+0x000` | `0x8003CA30` | 208 B | shell state entry: virtual `+0x2BC`, flag spans, pose copy, `+0x2C4`, `+0xD4` |
// | 3 | `0x80305F24` | `+0x00C` | `0x8003CDA0` | 40 B | release the `+0x5F0` sub-object, return `1` |
// | 8 | `0x80305F38` | `+0x020` | `0x8003CDD0` | 80 B | mode-2 `+0x5F0` reset, then forward to `0x80095480` |
// | 9 | `0x80305F3C` | `+0x024` | `0x8003CD60` | 48 B | forward to the `+0x544` model's `+0x14` slot, return `1` |
// | 16 | `0x80305F58` | `+0x040` | `0x8003D410` | 152 B | release/teardown: six sub-object releases, conditional `0x80162920` |
// | 58 | `0x80306000` | `+0x0E8` | `0x8003D060` | 168 B | two-mode attack/contact predicate through `+0x130`/`+0x134` |
// | 74 | `0x80306040` | `+0x128` | `0x8003D110` | 36 B | `0x80097E50` call, return `0` |
// | 75 | `0x80306044` | `+0x12C` | `0x8003D140` | 36 B | `0x80097EA0` call, return `0` |
// | 164 | `0x803061A8` | `+0x290` | `0x8003D2F0` | 120 B | `+0x694` gate, virtual `+0x2D8`/`+0x2D4`/`+0x2E8` |
// | 173 | `0x803061CC` | `+0x2B4` | `0x8003CB10` | 432 B | `daikonbou_long` model/animation builder (twin of [`fn_8001fa70`]) |
//
// None has a `functions.tsv` row, a Ghidra export or a ledger row; every
// evidence line cites raw words in `work/dol/main.elf` (disassembly in
// `work/wave265/e_dis.txt`). Extents are measured to the terminating `bclr`.
//
// Object map used below: `+0x04` actor flag word, `+0x24`/`+0x2D` contact
// record, `+0x60` class vtable, `+0xAC`/`+0xB0`/`+0xB4` position vector,
// `+0x500` angle/limit halfword, `+0x524` scratch buffer, `+0x540` archive,
// `+0x544` model, `+0x584`/`+0x588` first animation record and animation,
// `+0x5B4`/`+0x5B8` second animation and its record, `+0x5E4..+0x5EC` copied
// home position, `+0x5F0` sub-object, `+0x694`/`+0x698`/`+0x69C` state words.
//
// `no_std`; every call is an original callee reached by address.

