// ===========================================================================
// Wave 270 lane D - first twelve untabled methods of the 0x803017D0 vtable
// ===========================================================================
//
// `docs/UNTABLED_POINTER_TABLES.md` and `work/wave266/d_runs.tsv` list the run
// `0x803017D8..0x80301948` (92 slots, 45 uncovered at survey time, 12 of them
// prologue-shaped). Decoding the run gives the method half of one CodeWarrior
// vtable:
//
// * The header is the two zero words `0x803017D0`/`0x803017D4`; the method
//   array starts at `0x803017D8` and the word `0x80301948` is zero, i.e. the
//   table ends exactly where the next data record begins. The twelve bodies
//   below are the first twelve uncovered prologue-shaped targets in table
//   order (slots 0, 3, 6, 7, 16, 33, 61, 64, 67, 70, 73, 76).
// * All 92 entries are distinct code addresses in the two executable `PT_LOAD`
//   segments; none is an interior label. The targets span
//   `0x8001D1B0..0x801628B0` and cross the enemy/player/HUD bands, which is the
//   inherited-method vtable pattern, not a switch table.
// * The table is installed at object offset `+0x60` by three `d_basesNP`
//   constructors, `0x80659460`, `0x806EF6A0` and `0x8073B5C0` (already
//   translated in [`crate::game::bases`] as [`crate::game::bases::fn_80659460`],
//   [`crate::game::bases::fn_806ef6a0`] and
//   [`crate::game::bases::fn_8073b5c0`]). Each stores `0x803017D0` and then
//   overwrites it with its own derived REL vtable (`0x807E6698` /
//   `0x807FEB08` / `0x8080E900`), so `0x803017D0` is the shared base vtable.
// * Class identity: the four state descriptors in the same data block above
//   name `daBossDemo_c` - `daBossDemo_c::StateID_Ready`,
//   `::StateID_BattleStDemo`, `::StateID_BattleIn` and
//   `::StateID_BattleEdDemo` at `0x803016CF..0x80301753` - and the same data
//   block carries the `wipeKuppa`/`wipeMario` arc, layout and animation names
//   at `0x80301370..0x803014B8`, so this is the boss-intro demo actor that
//   plays those wipes.
// * Its own parent is the 77-slot vtable at `0x80301504` (methods from
//   `0x8030150C`): the first 77 slots of `0x803017D0` keep 44 of its words at
//   the same index, override 33 (the whole `54..76` block is replaced) and the
//   run adds fifteen new slots `77..91`. Slot 7 is the clearest case: the base
//   word is `0x800643F0` and the derived word is [`fn_8001dba0`], which calls
//   `0x800643F0` first.
// * Nothing materialises `0x803017D0` inside `main.dol`; the only absolute
//   references anywhere in the shipped files are the three `d_basesNP`
//   constructors. The wave-266
//   "owner" `0x8001E1C0` is itself slot 84 of the same table and only
//   materialises the `"Wm_en_hit"` string at `0x803017C0`, not the vtable, so
//   target containment in the materialising function is 0 of 92.
//
