// ===========================================================================
// Wave 271 lane E - parent vtable 0x80301504 (77 slots, daBossDemo_c base)
// ===========================================================================
//
// The 92-slot method run of `0x803017D0` (slots at `0x803017D8`) has a parent
// run at `0x80301504`. Decoding the whole run from `work/dol/main.elf` gives:
//
// * header: `0x80301504` and `0x80301508` are both zero (the CodeWarrior
//   `{0, 0}` vtable header); the 77 method words are
//   `0x8030150C..0x8030163C` and `0x80301640` is the terminating zero;
// * span: `0x80301504..0x80301644` (320 bytes, 8 header bytes + 77 methods +
//   terminator); the next data record begins at `0x80301644` with `0xE8`;
// * slots: 77, all distinct, all in the executable `PT_LOAD` segments;
// * containment: 0 of 77 targets lies strictly inside a tabulated function, so
//   no word is an interior label;
// * parent-vs-derived: comparing the parent word `i` with the derived word `i`
//   gives 44 identical words, 33 overrides and 15 appended derived slots
//   (`77..91`). The 33 overrides are slots
//   `0, 3, 6, 7, 9, 12, 16, 30, 33, 48, 54..76` - the whole tail from 54 on is
//   replaced, exactly as the wave-270 lane D report records.
//
// # Install site
//
// There is none. `0x803014FC..0x80301640` is not materialised by any `lis`/
// `addi`/`ori` pair or data word in `main.dol`, and the four shipped REL ELFs
// (`d_basesNP`, `d_enemiesNP`, `d_en_bossNP`, `d_profileNP`) contain no
// reference either. The wave-266 survey tag `materialised-outside-fn` is
// explained by the *adjacent* wipe descriptor base `0x803014E0`, named by
// `0x8001D2D4` and `0x8001D690` (both inside `0x8001D2C0`, the wipe-record
// initialiser), which sits 0x24 bytes before the header. The only nearby
// installer is the derived table: the three `d_basesNP` constructors
// `0x80659460`, `0x806EF6A0` and `0x8073B5C0` store `0x803017D0` at `+0x60`
// and immediately overwrite it with `0x807E6698` / `0x807FEB08` / `0x8080E900`.
// The parent run is therefore a linker-emitted base table, not a live
// per-object install in the shipped code.
//
// # Class identity
//
// The table is the base half of `daBossDemo_c`, whose concrete run is
// `0x803017D0`. The same data block names the class directly in
// `daBossDemo_c::StateID_Ready`, `::StateID_BattleStDemo`, `::StateID_BattleIn`
// and `::StateID_BattleEdDemo` at `0x803016CF..0x80301753`, and it carries the
// `wipeCircle` / `wipeDokan` / `wipeKuppa` / `wipeMario` asset names at
// `0x803011A0..0x803014B8`. The four wipe animation records built by
// `0x8001D2C0` live at `0x80352670`, `0x803526B0`, `0x803526F0` and
// `0x80352730` (stride `0x40`, file order Circle/Dokan/Kuppa/Mario, each with
// vtable `0x80301754` at record offset `+0`; the instruction is the
// `stw r30,0x18(r28)` displacement from the node base `0x80352658`); the
// bodies below hand records 0, 1 and 3 to the `+0x394` layout, which ties the
// table to the boss-intro wipe actor.
//
// # Extent note
//
// Extents below were followed by control flow. `bcctrl` (`0x4E800421`),
// conditional `bc` and conditional `bclr` fall through; only the closing
// unconditional `bclr 20,0` ends a path. Every extent includes that closing
// word and excludes the following zero alignment words.
//
// Only seven of the 29 uncovered slots are prologue-shaped
// (`0x8001CBF0`, `0x8001CCB0`, `0x8001D260`, `0x8001CF70`, `0x8001D090`,
// `0x8001D110`, `0x8001CE00`). All seven are translated here, together with
// five further uncovered leaves in table order (slots 3, 9, 12, 54 and 56),
// which completes the requested twelve.

/// `0x80352670`: wipe record 0 (Circle) of the four records built by
/// `0x8001D2C0`; its first word is the animation-record vtable `0x80301754`.
