// Wave 277, lane D (`_D277`): `daBullet_c` vtable `0x80301C00`
// ===========================================================================
//
// `0x80301C00` is a **166-slot class vtable**, not the state table the
// wave-227 inventory guessed. The decode is in `work/wave277/laneD_report.md`;
// the short form:
//
// | item | value |
// |---|---|
// | vtable header | `0x80301BF8 = 0`, `0x80301BFC = 0` |
// | method array | `0x80301C00..0x80301E98` (166 words, 664 bytes) |
// | following rodata | `0x80301E98` `"Wm_en_burst_s"`; next header `0x80301EA8` |
// | install site | `lis r4,0x8030` at `0x80A17180` + `addi r4,r4,0x1BF8` at
//   `0x80A17188`, `stw r4,0x60(r29)` inside the `d_enemiesNP` constructor
//   `0x80A17150`; the same pair appears at `0x80A17628`, `0x80A17A28` and
//   `0x80A17D78` in the sibling constructors `0x80A175F0`, `0x80A179F0` and
//   `0x80A17D40`. All four then overwrite `+0x60` with the concrete REL
//   vtable (`0x80B368F8`, `0x80B36BA8`, `0x80B36E58`, `0x80B37108`). |
//
// The four concrete `d_enemiesNP` vtables carry the same 166 words with 140/166
// entries identical to this array, so this is the shared base class; the
// `daBullet_c::StateID_*` name strings in the same `main.dol` rodata run
// (`0x80301A67..0x80301B57`) name the class.
//
// The eight prologue-shaped uncovered targets of the array - slots 0, 3, 6, 9,
// 16, 58, 74 and 75 - are translated below. They are filed in `ui::hud`
// because their bodies live in the `0x8001Fxxx`/`0x8002xxxx` band this module
// owns, as the lane brief requires; seven are ordinary virtual methods and the
// eighth (`0x80020700`) is the deleting destructor.
//
// | slot | word | target | extent | role |
// |---:|---|---|---|---|
// | 0 | `0x80301C00` | [`fn_8001f900`] | `0x8001F900..0x8001FA40` (320 B) | register the scene and build its model |
// | 3 | `0x80301C0C` | [`fn_8001fce0`] | `0x8001FCE0..0x8001FD38` (88 B) | release both animation holders and unregister |
// | 6 | `0x80301C18` | [`fn_8001fc50`] | `0x8001FC50..0x8001FC94` (68 B) | per-frame scene update |
// | 9 | `0x80301C24` | [`fn_8001fca0`] | `0x8001FCA0..0x8001FCD0` (48 B) | forward to the `+0x544` emitter's slot `+0x14` |
// | 16 | `0x80301C40` | [`fn_80020700`] | `0x80020700..0x80020798` (152 B) | deleting destructor |
// | 58 | `0x80301CE8` | [`fn_8001fe80`] | `0x8001FE80..0x8001FF28` (168 B) | two-step contact test through slots 74/75 |
// | 74 | `0x80301D28` | [`fn_8001ff30`] | `0x8001FF30..0x8001FF54` (36 B) | forward to `stage::fn_80097e50`, answer `0` |
// | 75 | `0x80301D2C` | [`fn_8001ff60`] | `0x8001FF60..0x8001FF84` (36 B) | forward to `stage::fn_80097ea0`, answer `0` |
//
// The eleven remaining uncovered slots are non-prologue leaves and stay out of
// this lane's quota: slot 12 `0x8001FCD0`, slots 159-164 `0x8001FA40`,
// `0x8001FA50`, `0x8001FA60`, `0x8001FE40`, `0x80020390`, `0x800203B0` (bare
// `blr`), slot 158 `0x8001F890` and slot 56 `0x8001FE50` (`li r3,0` / `blr`),
// slot 60 `0x8001FE60` (`lwz r4,4(r5)` then tail-dispatch to vtable `+0x220`)
// and slot 165 `0x800203A0` (`lfs f1,[r2-0x7E18]` / `blr`).
