// ===========================================================================
// Wave 285 lane A (`_A285`): the last eighteen uncovered methods of the
// `daEnDoor_c` base vtable `0x80303658`
// ===========================================================================
//
// ## Shape and identity
//
// The run `0x80303660..0x8030390C` is a 171-word method array (684 bytes). The
// eight bytes before it, `0x80303658`/`0x8030365C`, are both zero: the standard
// two-word class header (`offset-to-top`, `typeinfo`) that precedes every
// NSMBW vtable. The stored class word is therefore `0x80303658` and the first
// method is `0x80303660`; `[[this+0x60] + 8 + 4*slot]` is the dispatch form
// used by the rest of this band. The `word`/`offset` columns below are relative
// to the array base `0x80303660`, while the raw displacements quoted in the
// bodies (`+0x280` for slot 158, `+0x294` for slot 163, ...) are measured from
// the stored header and therefore exceed the array offset by eight.
//
// The class is `daEnDoor_c`, the door-actor base. Three independent pieces of
// shipped evidence fix the identity:
//
// * the five state descriptors this class dispatches through `+0xD4` -
//   `0x80352FD0`/`0x80353010`/`0x80353050`/`0x80353090`/`0x803530D0` - are
//   documented as `daEnDoor_c::StateID_*` in
//   [`crate::boot::init_tables::fn_8002b8c0`], the class's `.ctors` body;
// * the array ends exactly at `0x8030390C`, where the five nine-word state
//   parameter blocks start (`0x8030390C..0x803039C0`), followed by the five
//   `"daEnDoor_c::StateID_..."` strings;
// * every `d_enemiesNP` door subclass vtable is a verbatim 171-word copy of
//   this array with a handful of overrides - `0x80B5B7E0` (`obj_obake_door`),
//   `0x80B45200` (`obj_doorA`) and the rest - so this is the immediate base
//   class of the `obj_*door*` family.
//
// The literal immediately before the header, `"Wm_en_obakedoor"` at
// `0x80303648..0x80303658`, is the effect name used by the open-door helper
// [`fn_8002b590`] in the same translation unit. It is *not* RTTI: the
// `daEnDpakkunBase_c` table `0x80304494` is preceded the same way by
// `"dead_ice"`, and the REL door tables are preceded by their sprite names.
//
// ## Install sites
//
// No `lis`/`addi` pair in `main.dol` materialises either `0x80303658` or
// `0x80303660`, and no data word holds them. The header word is installed only
// by the intermediate `stw` in six `d_enemiesNP` constructors, always at
// `+0x60` and always immediately replaced by the subclass's own table:
//
// | constructor | extent | writes | final class vtable |
// |---|---|---|---|
// | `0x80A31980` | 156 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B5B7D8` (`obj_obake_door`) |
// | `0x80A52980` | 156 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B451E8` (`obj_doorA`) |
// | `0x80AAFD10` | 240 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B548C4` |
// | `0x80AD2A20` | 156 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B6B7D8` |
// | `0x80B0A410` | 160 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B675AC` |
// | `0x80B15330` | 156 B | `+0x30` | `0x80B798B0` |
//
// All six are the inlined base-constructor `vptr` store, so the base table is
// live only for the duration of the base constructor. That is why the array
// carries no data reference of its own.
//
// ## Containment
//
// `0x80303648..0x80303658` is the `"Wm_en_obakedoor"` literal (15 chars + NUL,
// flush against the header). `0x8030390C..0x803039C0` is the five nine-word
// state-parameter region and `0x803039C0..` the five state-name strings. No
// slot crosses either boundary, every one of the 171 targets is a distinct
// main-DOL text address, and none of the eighteen below lies inside a
// `functions.tsv` row or a translated extent.
//
// ## Census
